{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 40, :comments ["<b>On the first day.</b> Is it really first? Is it not the 15th? Rather, it is first for the reckoning of iniquities, as is stated in the midrash: on Yom HaKippurim all is forgiven; from here onward, this one is occupied with his sukkah and that one with his lulav; on the day of Sukkot they come and praise before HaKadosh Baruch Hu, and He says to them: I have pardoned you for all that was from here onward — reckoned." "<b>Fruit of a hadar tree.</b> Some of them produce fruit and some of them do not produce fruit, and they are in one bundle — to tell you that the righteous and the intermediate should join together to do the will of their Creator." "<b>And you shall rejoice seven days.</b> Because each and every day is a festival in itself, and the offerings prove it."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:14:49.544667171Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}